# Cargo build output.
target/

# Cargo.lock IS committed (see core/Cargo.lock). Convention says a library omits it;
# this repo's rule is stronger and applies here for the same reason `pnpm-lock.yaml`
# is committed and enforced by a pre-push hook: a dependency resolved fresh on every
# CI run is a dependency nobody chose. The lockfile is what makes "the tests passed"
# a statement about a specific set of code.

# Tauri writes gen/schemas/ during the build, and the file set is PLATFORM-SPECIFIC
# (linux-schema.json here, windows-schema.json on the Windows runner). Committing it
# would mean the tree drifts depending on which machine last built — the same trap as
# a committed lockfile that gets regenerated per platform.
app/gen/

# The cargo test log CI tees for scripts/check-desktop-core-tests.mjs; a local run
# must not leave it as an untracked file that dirties the tree.
test-output.txt
